```

## Pre-Commit Checklist

**Before `git commit` on any builder/ change:**

- [ ] Build script exists for this version
- [ ] Build script ran successfully
- [ ] Record count validation passed
- [ ] Layer size validation passed
- [ ] Critical field decompression passed
- [ ] Field checksums match reference (if applicable)
- [ ] Smoke test completed (or documented why skipped)
- [ ] manifest.json updated with new pack
- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated

**Agent workflow:**
1. Agent writes build script
2. Agent runs build script (validation included)
3. Agent commits script + layer + manifest
4. Agent pushes to builder
5. **User downloads and playtests** (final validation)

## Red Flags (STOP and Fix)

❌ Record count >2x expected → Corruption or wrong build  
❌ Layer size >2x expected → Bloat or duplication  
❌ Any field decompression failure → LZS corruption  
❌ Checksum mismatch vs reference → Wrong field bytes  
❌ "Skipping validation" in build logs → Not allowed

## What Happens on Validation Failure

**DO NOT commit the layer.**

1. Investigate why validation failed
2. Fix the build script
3. Re-run build + validation
4. Only commit when all checks pass

**DO NOT:**
- Commit broken layer and "fix later"
- Lower thresholds to make validation pass
- Skip validation "just this once"
- Guess at fixes without understanding root cause

## Integration with Other Rules

- **build-automation.mdc:** Build scripts include validation
